WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:02.869
You wrote a detection as a file,

3
00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:06.300
in Microsoft Learn's shape,
with its status disabled.

4
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.103
You tested its query against a
thirty-day validation window,

5
00:00:10.103 --> 00:00:12.537
and saved the result as its test record.

6
00:00:12.537 --> 00:00:14.887
You deployed it through
Graph, read it back,

7
00:00:14.887 --> 00:00:17.975
and compared everything
deployed with the repository.

8
00:00:17.975 --> 00:00:20.484
And you ran the cross-source
query that finds

9
00:00:20.484 --> 00:00:22.925
a user with alerts from
more than one source.

10
00:00:22.925 --> 00:00:25.834
The evidence an I S S O
keeps from this module:

11
00:00:25.834 --> 00:00:30.601
the detection repository at a tagged
commit, each rule's test output, the

12
00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:34.156
deployed-rules export, the
correlation query output,

13
00:00:34.156 --> 00:00:36.337
and the identity sensors' health.

14
00:00:36.337 --> 00:00:40.682
Next is Module 5, the last:
automation with approval boundaries,

15
00:00:40.682 --> 00:00:44.330
the operating cadence, and
the monthly evidence run.
